  "name": "Magic",
  "abstract": "Wallet-as-a-service platform from the USA that adds passwordless authentication and non-custodial wallets to web3 and consumer apps. Embedded Wallets log users in with email OTP, SMS, social login, passkeys, Farcaster or an external wallet and give each of them a wallet on 30+ blockchains, using sharded keys in trusted execution environments. SDKs cover web, React Native, iOS, Android and Flutter, with Node.js and Python Admin SDKs, and Server Wallets (Express and Core APIs) let backends and agents sign transactions with JWTs from an existing identity provider. Magic is not an OpenID Provider and returns DID tokens instead. The Developer plan includes 1,000 monthly active wallets. SaaS-only.",
